cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Cosmic Atlas, please cite it as below, and cite the surveys whose data you used (see README and each layer's PROVENANCE.json)."
title: "Cosmic Atlas: a 3D map of the real universe in the browser"
type: software
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24224239"
authors:
  - alias: ismoilovdevml
repository-code: "https://github.com/ismoilovdevml/cosmic-atlas"
url: "https://ismoilovdevml.github.io/cosmic-atlas/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A browser 3D map of the universe built only from open survey data: the Solar System at its
  real positions, Gaia DR3 stars, 3D dust, star clusters, the Local Group,
  15 million DESI DR1 galaxies and quasars, gravitational-wave localisation volumes, FRBs,
  neutrinos and the Planck CMB, streamed as octree tiles with distance uncertainty and a cited
  source for every number. WebGPU, with a WebGL2 fallback; interface and articles in Uzbek,
  English and Russian.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - astrophysics
  - data visualization
  - Gaia
  - DESI
  - cosmology
  - WebGPU
  - 3D map
